      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A high-level executive's physical presence can include a tall, majestic stature, direct posture, and crisp, clean attire. They should also possess distinct communication nuances like an authoritative tone of voice, with a slight upward inflection at the end of sentences to convey confidence and conviction. Additionally, leaders with high-level authority tend to use expansive, gestural speech, often drawing on familiar anecdotes and trusting authority to connect with audiences. They also tend to listen attentively, using subtle negative head nods and brief pauses to convey empathy and interest.",
